<title>INDIA: India commodities markets shut in tax hike protest.</title>
<headline>India commodities markets shut in tax hike protest.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Most Indian commodities markets were shut on Thursday in a protest called by traders against a tax hike by authorities in Bombay, the country's commercial capital, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said the strike affected bullion, cotton, metals, castor and sugar markets. Trading will resume on Friday.</p>
<p>Traders are protesting the increase in sales tax and other charges from January 1 by the government in the western Maharashtra state, where Bombay is located.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22 265 9000</p>
</text>
